        <rule id="de7a-0114-c47f-9e75" name="Unit rules / draft status" hidden="false">
          <description>3rd Company dedicated void-breach and shipboard infantry
DRAFT Breach Sequence: once per battle, when this unit declares a Charge against an enemy wholly within terrain, add 1 to its Charge roll. Approved universal passive Ghost-Shroud, Sergeant Ghost-Sight. Q34 advanced module does NOT automatically apply merely because this is 3rd Company.</description>
        </rule>
      <rule id="5462eb7f-fb4e-58a7-b495" name="Where to find weapons (v1.8)" hidden="false"><description>Open Squad Size / Personnel, then the selected size, then each named model. Five (or ten) required models and their standard weapons now populate automatically. Change each model’s Primary Weapon choice to make legal replacements; optional sixth–ninth models must be added deliberately. Equipment is charged once per selected model; do not add a second separate weapon copy.</description></rule><rule id="f3a0a7ff-34a5-517d-a28b" name="Breach Sequence" hidden="false"><description>once per battle, when this unit declares a Charge against an enemy wholly within terrain, add 1 to its Charge roll. Approved universal passive Ghost-Shroud, Sergeant Ghost-Sight. Q34 advanced module does NOT automatically apply merely because this is 3rd Company.</description></rule></rules>
      <rules>
        <rule id="2a53-ff33-0e2f-fc47" name="Ghost-Shroud (passive; approved)" hidden="false">
          <description>Hidden detection 12" instead of 15". When exposed and not fired this or preceding turn and not Advanced/Charged, has Stealth. Does not automatically gain Hidden.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <rules>
        <rule id="2337-1b03-3668-4184" name="Ghost-Sight Sergeant Targeting Uplink (approved)" hidden="false">
          <description>Once per your Shooting phase, living Sergeant chooses one enemy visible to them. Other models in own unit re-roll ranged Hit rolls of 1 vs that unit. No illegal targeting or rerolling a die twice.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <rules>
